      "message": "\"Return True deterministically for any flag name.\n\n    Pure function of its argument: no I/O, no randomness, no time, no state.\n    \"\"\"\n    return True\n\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    assert feature_flag() is True\n    assert feature_flag(\"anything\") is True\n    assert CONFIG_NAME\n    print(CONFIG_NAME, feature_flag())\n```\n\nNotes:\n- `feature_flag()` is a pure, deterministic predicate that always returns the boolean `True`, accepting an optional flag-name argument and ignoring it.\n- `CONFIG_NAME` is a module-level string constant.\n- It imports nothing, is self-contained, and has no dependency on `semkg_contract` or any other module.\n\nLocal check: I attempted a small sanity run, but the Python runner sandbox does not expose the written file at the expected path (it runs from a different temporary working directory), so the verification attempt failed with `FileNotFoundError` rather than exercising the module. No other files were created or modified by me; the check produced no artifacts."
